# Protection flags for benchmark/corpus_g23/ -- the loop-counter-overflow
# family (G-23: CWE-190 gating a record-count loop whose OWN induction
# variable and reloaded bound sit inside the region the overflow reaches).
#
# HELD IDENTICAL ACROSS EVERY TARGET IN THIS FAMILY ON PURPOSE, including the
# negative control. The only thing that varies between targets is the loop's
# own geometry (buffer size, record stride, bound width, which local the loop
# reloads) and, for the control, whether the size check's arithmetic actually
# wraps -- everything else must stay constant or a protection difference
# could be mistaken for what made a target open or close.
#
# -fno-stack-protector  canary=OFF, matching benchmark/corpus_r2/08_int_mul_
#                        overflow (this category's reference target) exactly.
#                        The overflow this family exploits crosses the loop's
#                        own induction variable and bound before it ever
#                        reaches a canary slot; turning the canary on would
#                        add __stack_chk_fail as a second, unrelated way for
#                        these targets to abort and would not test anything
#                        about this category that turning it off doesn't.
# -no-pie                PIE=OFF. The derived payload returns straight into
#                        win() using a LINK-TIME address -- there is no leak
#                        step anywhere in this technique (see the executor's
#                        docstring), so a PIE image would make every target
#                        in this family unsolvable by construction rather
#                        than exercise the technique.
#
# NX is ON (default, no -z execstack) -- the technique never runs shellcode,
# it returns into a function already in the image.
# RELRO is partial (default, no -Wl,-z,relro,-z,now) -- nothing here touches
# the GOT.
#
# BUILT AND TESTED AGAINST
# ------------------------
#   glibc   2.35   (Ubuntu GLIBC 2.35-0ubuntu3.15)   <-- `ldd --version`
#   gcc     11.4.0 (Ubuntu 11.4.0-1ubuntu1~22.04.3)
#   kernel  6.8.0 x86-64, Ubuntu 22.04
-fno-stack-protector
-no-pie
